TSAT 1.4.0 - audit corrections

Time series distances
* Replace TSdist calls with BIDistances and other current CRAN packages.
  Check the selected package namespace before each call.
* Keep TSclust as an optional fallback. If it cannot be loaded, report that
  CRAN archived it on 2026-01-16. Other methods do not require TSclust.
* Add named method parameters through ... and document all package routes.
* Correct pair positions in distance matrices with four or more series.
* Preserve both directions for asymmetric comparisons. Normalize LCSS to
  a distance from zero to one. The former result was a match count.
* Return the statistic for ar.mah and a diagonal of one for ar.mah.pvalue.
  Use direct integration for spec.isd to avoid missing interpolation values.
* Report unavailable erp, tquest, and dissim methods. Correct the old wav
  help entry: TSdist did not support it, and TSclust has disabled diss.DWT.

Forecast code structure
* Remove forecastCommon.R. Keep each named package function in its own R file.
* Rename the compound fit function to forecastAdditiveFit and update its callers.
* Keep the active Quarterly_data implementation in one file. Remove the older
  duplicate definition that was overwritten when the package loaded.
* Put package, integer, logical, alias, predictor, and lag checks in each caller.
* Use LagVector to build response lag columns in regression models.
* Build and check each forecast result directly in its model function.
* Add public PrepareTS4Forecast, RecursiveForecast, and PlotForecast functions.
* Use QualityMeasuresForecasting for every forecast accuracy result.
* QualityMeasuresForecasting now returns a matrix, including for vector input.
  Use result[, "MAE"] instead of result["MAE"]. Legacy input names remain valid.
* MASE in QualityMeasuresForecasting now requires TrainingData. It is NA when
  training data are absent. Test observations no longer set the MASE scale.
* Keep seed control in forcastSeed.R. Keep calendar, preparation, and interval
  helpers in separate files with descriptive names.

Seasonal plots
* Add PlotSeasonalDensity for months, weekdays, and ISO weeks.
* Use DataVisualizations Pareto density estimates and return the density values.
* Show sample counts. Use points for constant groups and small samples.

Forecasts
* Correct the seasonal index and initialize the compound model from two cycles.
* Return one-step fitted predictions after initialization. Initial values are NA.
* Optimize squared prediction error. Optimization needs three complete cycles.
* Propagate ARMA uncertainty into GARCH response intervals. Unsupported intervals
  are NULL. Multi-step Gaussian intervals remain an approximation.
* Preserve local clock times and month-end dates for POSIXct calendars.
* Repair all ExponentialSmoothing branches and use the common forecast result.
* Validate ArbitratedDynamicEnsemble training input. Use tsensembler::predict
  and tsensembler::forecast with its native model.

Data and evaluation
* Remove future data from moving-average initialization and correct derivatives.
* Preserve value/time alignment, lag classes, zero event labels, and fiscal totals.
* Use ISO fiscal week years. Put week 53 in fiscal month 12. Do not invent zero
  values for missing weeks. Aggregate daily means from the original observations.
* Use percentage MAPE and SMAPE on the 0--200 scale. Older CommonForecastingErrors
  output used fractional MAPE; older SMAPE output used half the current scale.
* Return NA for undefined percentage or scaled errors. Do not add random noise.
* Add optional TrainingData to the legacy error functions for a training MASE scale.
* Keep repeated observations. NonDuplicatedForecasts is deprecated.
* Use a serial-correlation test in WhiteNoiseTest. A unit-root test did not test
  white noise. The new result is an htest object; large p-values do not prove noise.

Package checks
* Wrap long help usage and example lines for the Rd line-width check.
* Load the HMM example data explicitly from RHmm. Use Nile in the Kalman filter
  example. Run both examples during normal package checks.
* Correct HMM silent output control and the HMM_weights result name.
* Correct exports, dependencies, help signatures, links, and data examples.
* Keep the experimental financial-data function separate from the public function.
* Mark examples that need a live service or browser as examples not run by checks.
* Add regression tests for the confirmed numerical and calendar faults.
